      "message": "fix(mcp): the cli dials a ui link file only while its window holds its lock\n\nA stale discovery file let a false server on the freed port of a crashed\nwindow receive the CLI's tool calls: whoever reads the file can compute\nevery token proof. Each window now holds an exclusive OS file lock on\n<pid>.lock for its whole life (std File::try_lock; the OS releases it at\nany exit). The CLI tests the lock before it dials an entry and again\nafter the hello. A free lock marks the file stale: it is removed and\nlogged, never dialed. A file with no lock to test is skipped and logged,\nnever a silent fall-back. No new dependency.\n\nThe Windows named-pipe transport (peer process check) stays a follow-up.\n\nRefs #3995\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
